+  // Gtavport (docs/validacao-18-11.md): why each new pipeline compiles. In the Turnip the shaders' key is the VS+PS pair
+  // (and GS) plus the spec constants; target format, blend and vertex layout are not in it (~0.1 ms). So a new pipeline
+  // is: a PS never seen, a known PS with a new partner, a known pair with another spec (the render-scale bit or other
+  // bits), or a known pair+spec with other state only. Counted with the compile time, logged as [pipe].
+  struct PipeClasses {
+    std::unordered_set<uint64_t> ps, pair, pair_spec;
+    uint32_t n[5] = {};
+    double ms[5] = {};
+    uint64_t last_log = 0;
